/-!
# VIII08 — the four far-field limits of the rotation

`sigma_b` is the actual limit of `R b_s(R)`.  Its consequences for `v` are:

* `R³ (v - j/R²) = (1/u³) ∫₀^u t² h(t) dt` with `u = 1/R` and
  `h(t) = 6·(b_s(1/t)/(1/t)) - r(t)`, `h(0) = 6 sigma_b - r(0)`.
  Hence `R³(v - j/R²) → h(0)/3 = 2 sigma_b - r(0)/3`.
* `R² v = j + (R³(v - j/R²))/R → j`.
* `R⁴(v' + 2j/R³) = r(1/R) - 6 R b_s(R) → r(0) - 6 sigma_b`.
-/

